  about: {
    title: "About – Shreechakra Mandiram",
    html: "<div class=\"page-hero\">\r\n  <p class=\"breadcrumb\"><a href=\"index.html\">Home</a> · About</p>\r\n  <h1>Our Sacred Heritage</h1>\r\n  <p>A temple born from devotion, sustained by tradition, and alive through the grace of Devi Tripura Sundari.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<!-- MISSION -->\r\n<section class=\"section\">\r\n  <div class=\"container two-col\">\r\n    <div class=\"fade-in\">\r\n      <p class=\"section-label\">Our Purpose</p>\r\n      <h2>Why Shreechakra Mandiram Exists</h2>\r\n      <p style=\"color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:1rem;\">The Shreechakra — the sacred geometric diagram of the Divine Mother — is considered the most powerful of all yantras in the Shakta tradition. Our temple was founded with a singular purpose: to make this living science accessible to sincere devotees, and to maintain an unbroken tradition of its worship.</p>\r\n      <p style=\"color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:1rem;\">We are not merely a place of religious ritual, but a living university of spiritual wisdom, where the Vedic, Tantric, and Puranic streams converge in service of the Divine Mother.</p>\r\n      <p style=\"color:var(--text-muted);\">Every stone, every ritual, every mantra here is calibrated to the sacred geometry of the Shreechakra, making this entire space a three-dimensional yantra.</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"about-visual fade-in\" style=\"display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;\">\r\n      <div style=\"text-align:center;padding:2rem;\">\r\n        <div style=\"font-size:5rem;margin-bottom:1rem;\">🙏</div>\r\n        <div style=\"font-family:var(--font-sub);color:var(--gold-lt);font-size:0.85rem;letter-spacing:0.15em;text-transform:uppercase;\">Established</div>\r\n        <div style=\"font-family:var(--font-head);font-size:3rem;color:var(--gold);\">1973</div>\r\n        <div style=\"width:60px;height:1px;background:var(--gold-dk);margin:1rem auto;\"></div>\r\n        <div style=\"font-family:var(--font-sub);color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.9rem;\">Over 50 years of<br>unbroken worship</div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</section>\r\n\r\n<!-- HISTORY TIMELINE -->\r\n<section class=\"section\" style=\"background:var(--bg-section)\">\r\n  <div class=\"container\">\r\n    <p class=\"section-label\">Temple History</p>\r\n    <h2>Five Decades of Devotion</h2>\r\n    <div class=\"timeline\">\r\n      <div class=\"timeline-item fade-in\">\r\n        <div class=\"timeline-year\">1973</div>\r\n        <div class=\"timeline-content\">\r\n          <h4>Founding & Consecration</h4>\r\n          <p>Sri Pandit Ramachandra Shastri, a renowned Shakta scholar from Varanasi, consecrated the original Shreechakra yantra on Navaratri Mahanavami, establishing the first puja in a humble shed. The presiding deity, Devi Rajeshwari, was installed following Tantric tradition.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n      <div class=\"timeline-item fade-in\">\r\n        <div class=\"timeline-year\">1985</div>\r\n        <div class=\"timeline-content\">\r\n          <h4>Main Temple Structure Built</h4>\r\n          <p>With community support, the current granite temple was constructed following Agama Shastra guidelines. The gopuram was consecrated by Shankaracharya Sri Abhinava Vidyatirtha Mahaswami during his historic Bangalore visit.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n      <div class=\"timeline-item fade-in\">\r\n        <div class=\"timeline-year\">1998</div>\r\n        <div class=\"timeline-content\">\r\n          <h4>The Great Kumbhabhishekam</h4>\r\n          <p>A 10-day Maha Kumbhabhishekam was conducted with over 108 priests from across South India. The Shodasha Mahabhishekam of the Devi and the renovation of the Shreechakra yantra renewed the divine presence of the temple.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n      <div class=\"timeline-item fade-in\">\r\n        <div class=\"timeline-year\">2010</div>\r\n        <div class=\"timeline-content\">\r\n          <h4>Cultural & Educational Wing</h4>\r\n          <p>The Shakti Vidyapeetha was established — offering courses in Vedic chanting, Sanskrit, Indian classical music, and Yantra Shastra. Over 500 students have graduated from these programs.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n      <div class=\"timeline-item fade-in\">\r\n        <div class=\"timeline-year\">2023</div>\r\n        <div class=\"timeline-content\">\r\n          <h4>Golden Jubilee Celebration</h4>\r\n          <p>The 50th anniversary was celebrated with a grand 21-day Ati Rudra Maha Yagna, Sahasra Deepotsava, and the installation of a newly carved Panchadhatu Shreechakra Meru — gifted by devotees from 12 countries.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</section>\r\n\r\n<!-- PRIESTS -->\r\n<section class=\"section\">\r\n  <div class=\"container\">\r\n    <p class=\"section-label center\">Our Spiritual Guides</p>\r\n    <h2 class=\"center\">The Temple's Priestly Lineage</h2>\r\n    <div class=\"cards-grid\" style=\"margin-top:3rem;\">\r\n      <div class=\"feature-card fade-in\" style=\"text-align:center;\">\r\n        <div style=\"font-size:3.5rem;margin-bottom:1rem;\">👳</div>\r\n        <h3 style=\"font-family:var(--font-sub);color:var(--gold-lt);margin-bottom:0.3rem;\">Sri Subrahmanya Shastri</h3>\r\n        <span style=\"font-family:var(--font-sub);font-size:0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:var(--gold);text-transform:uppercase;display:block;margin-bottom:0.8rem;\">Head Priest · Agama Vaidika</span>\r\n        <p style=\"color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.9rem;\">A third-generation Shakta priest with 35 years of experience in Sri Vidya Upasana and Shodashopachara Puja. Trained under the Sringeri Sharada Peetham lineage.</p>\r\n      </div>\r\n      <div class=\"feature-card fade-in\" style=\"text-align:center;\">\r\n        <div style=\"font-size:3.5rem;margin-bottom:1rem;\">👳</div>\r\n        <h3 style=\"font-family:var(--font-sub);color:var(--gold-lt);margin-bottom:0.3rem;\">Sri Venkataraman Dikshitar</h3>\r\n        <span style=\"font-family:var(--font-sub);font-size:0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:var(--gold);text-transform:uppercase;display:block;margin-bottom:0.8rem;\">Chief Tantrik · Mantra Shastra</span>\r\n        <p style=\"color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.9rem;\">Specialises in Tantra Prayoga and Homa Vidhi. A scholar of Lalita Sahasranama with deep expertise in Mantra Shastra and Yantra Puja.</p>\r\n      </div>\r\n      <div class=\"feature-card fade-in\" style=\"text-align:center;\">\r\n        <div style=\"font-size:3.5rem;margin-bottom:1rem;\">👳</div>\r\n        <h3 style=\"font-family:var(--font-sub);color:var(--gold-lt);margin-bottom:0.3rem;\">Sri Krishnamurthy Bhatt</h3>\r\n        <span style=\"font-family:var(--font-sub);font-size:0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:var(--gold);text-transform:uppercase;display:block;margin-bottom:0.8rem;\">Assistant Priest · Vedic Rites</span>\r\n        <p style=\"color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.9rem;\">Expert in Vedic Yajna procedures and Pancharatra Agama. Leads the Sandhyavandanam and daily Naivedyam rituals with unwavering discipline.</p>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</section>\r\n\r\n<!-- BELIEFS -->\r\n<section class=\"quote-section\">\r\n  <div class=\"quote-inner\">\r\n    <div class=\"quote-chakra\">⬡</div>\r\n    <blockquote>\"The Shreechakra is not merely a diagram. It is a living map of consciousness — the universe encoded in geometry. To worship it is to worship the Devi in her most essential, most infinite form.\"</blockquote>\r\n    <cite>— Sri Subrahmanya Shastri, Head Priest</cite>\r\n  </div>\r\n</section>"
  },
